      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Taking a step off\" doesn't mean stopping completely, but rather finding a way to intentionally pause the frantic energy and look at the structure of the problem. This might involve a drastic, temporary reduction in spending or prioritizing one area of debt to create a small breathing room. You are right that the system feels rigged, but even a small pause can give you the clarity to make a calculated move against it.",
      "source": "target",
