    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but even a \"small breathing room\" is just a temporary fix, isnt it? i'm talkin about the long term. the math stays the same. interest gets higher, inflation goes up, and i just get older and more tired. it feels less like a problem i can solve and more like a sentence i'm serving. i don't see how any \"calculated move\" changes the fact that i am just existentially underwater. its like trying to bail out the ocean with a spoon.",
