      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's true that the large systems feel insurmountable, like trying to bail out an ocean with a spoon. When the whole structure feels like a sentence, the focus shifts from \"fixing\" it to finding a way to *escape* the sentence entirely. This might mean looking beyond incremental changes and seriously considering options for a complete break, like finding a different kind of work or seeking out a more fundamental change in your living situation. Sometimes, the most effective move isn't a small patch, but a complete redirection of the entire course.",
      "source": "target",
